.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt OPENSSL-VERSION 1ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm openssl-version
.Nd print OpenSSL version information
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm openssl version
.Oo
.Fl help ]
.Oo
.Fl a ]
.Oo
.Fl v ]
.Oo
.Fl b ]
.Oo
.Fl o ]
.Oo
.Fl f ]
.Oo
.Fl p ]
.Oo
.Fl d ]
.Oo
.Fl e ]
.Oo
.Fl m ]
.Oo
.Fl r ]
.Oo
.Fl c ]
.Oo
.Fl w ]
.Sh DESCRIPTION
This command is used to print out version information about OpenSSL.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy -help
Print out a usage message.
.It Sy -a
All information, this is the same as setting all the other flags.
.It Sy -v
The current OpenSSL version.
.It Sy -b
The date the current version of OpenSSL was built.
.It Sy -o
Option information: various options set when the library was built.
.It Sy -f
Compilation flags.
.It Sy -p
Platform setting.
.It Sy -d
OPENSSLDIR setting.
.It Sy -e
ENGINESDIR settings.
.It Sy -m
MODULESDIR settings.
.It Sy -r
The random number generator source settings.
.It Sy -c
The OpenSSL CPU settings info.
.It Sy -w
The OpenSSL
.Sy OSSL_WINCTX
build time variable, if set.
Used for computing Windows registry key names.
This option is unavailable on non-Windows platforms.
.El
.Sh HISTORY
In OpenSSL versions prior to 3.4, OpenSSL had a limitation regarding the
.Sy OPENSSLDIR ,
.Sy MODULESDIR
and
.Sy ENGINESDIR
build time macros.
These macros were defined at build time, and represented filesystem
paths.
This is common practice on unix like systems, as there was an
expectation that a given build would be installed to a pre-determined
location.
On Windows however, there is no such expectation, as libraries can be
installed to arbitrary locations.
.Sy OSSL_WINCTX
was introduced as a new build time variable to define a set of registry
keys identified by the name openssl-<version>-<ctx>, in which the
<version> value is derived from the version string in the openssl
source, and the <ctx> extension is derived from the
.Sy OSSL_WINCTX
variable.
The values of
.Sy OPENSSLDIR ,
.Sy ENGINESDIR
and
.Sy MODULESDIR
can be set to various paths underneath this key to break the requirement
to predict the installation path at build time.
.Sh NOTES
The output of
.Qo Li openssl version -a Qc
would typically be used when sending in a bug report.
